Let's update backend. We are going to distinguish between session (contains live session, i.e. messages for particular session thread and this is stored in redis - current implementation) and conversation history.

Conversation history holds all the user conversation in a form of JSON with all metadata needed in CosmosDB object database. Every conversation has ID key (probably threadid or our session id) to be uniquely identifiable for each user.

For dev purposes we will use locall a CosmosDB emulator - image is already available:

Run Cosmos DB Emulator in Docker (Linux)
docker run
--name cosmos-emulator
--detach
--publish 8081:8081
--publish 1234:1234
mcr.microsoft.com/cosmosdb/linux/azure-cosmos-emulator:vnext-preview

Let's add these vars to env:

Environment variables for Cosmos
COSMOS_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8081/
COSMOS_KEY=C2y6yDjf5/R+ob0N8A7Cgv30VRDJIWEHLM+4QDU5DE2nQ9nDuVTqobD4b8mGGyPMbIZnqyMsEcaGQy67XIw/Jw==
COSMOS_DATABASE_NAME=conversationhistory
COSMOS_CONTAINER_NAME=conversationhistory

Temporary: disable SSL verification for local Cosmos DB Emulator (remove when cert trusted)
COSMOS_EMULATOR_DISABLE_SSL_VERIFY=1

Let's create plan and design first, no coding now.